  "help:sweepBandMode": "Choose a common or per-channel sweep range. Off uses 20 Hz to 20 kHz for ESS, limited by the actual sample rate. Per Channel lets you set each selected output separately.",
  "label:sweepMinFreq": "Sweep Minimum Frequency (Hz):", // Label for sweep minimum frequency
  "help:sweepMinFreq": "The minimum frequency of the sweep signal in Hz. Set from 1 Hz up to just below the Nyquist frequency of the selected sampling rate. The test signal is also band-limited to this range. The speaker distortion test signal is limited to the same range. (Default: 20 Hz)", // Help text for sweep min frequency
  "label:sweepMaxFreq": "Sweep Maximum Frequency (Hz):", // Label for sweep maximum frequency
  "help:sweepMaxFreq": "The maximum frequency of the sweep signal in Hz. Values above the Nyquist frequency of the selected sampling rate are automatically clamped. The test signal is also band-limited to this range. The speaker distortion test signal is limited to the same range. (Default: 20000 Hz)", // Help text for sweep max frequency
  "label:averaging": "Synchronous Averaging:", // Label for synchronous averaging selection
  "help:averaging": "Number of repeats at the same point. Each repeat includes the sweep and 2.5 seconds for the response to decay, so more repeats take longer.",
